# Task 2 - Customer Segmentation Using K-Means Clustering

## Project Overview

This project focuses on customer segmentation using Machine Learning techniques as part of the SkillCraft Technology Machine Learning Internship.

The goal is to group customers into different segments based on their characteristics and purchasing behavior using the K-Means Clustering algorithm.

## Objective

* Analyze customer data.
* Apply K-Means Clustering to identify customer groups.
* Visualize the clusters to understand customer patterns.

## Technologies Used

* Python
* Pandas
* NumPy
* Matplotlib
* Scikit-learn

## Methodology

1. Load and explore the dataset.
2. Clean and preprocess the data.
3. Select relevant features for clustering.
4. Apply the K-Means Clustering algorithm.
5. Visualize and interpret the resulting clusters.

## Results

The clustering results help identify groups of customers with similar characteristics. The number and interpretation of clusters depend on the dataset and model results.

## Files

* `SCT_ML_Task2_Customer_Segmentation.ipynb` - Notebook containing the code and analysis.
* Dataset files or result visualizations, if appropriate.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates how unsupervised Machine Learning can be used to segment customers and discover patterns in customer data.

